> >>> this problem
> >>>> is specific to my setup, or if it is a real bug. Can anyone else=20
> >>>> out there running x86_64 confirm or deny this behavior?
>
> I currently have my fingers on a box with 2.6.23.14 with=20
> Xenomai 2.4.1 and I-pipe 1.4-01 (all standard), but I'm not=20
> able to reproduce your effect. Some simple shell loop nicely=20
> loads one CPU at 100%, and /proc/stat looks like this:
>=20
> cpu  38794 0 6325 411304 2882 0 3265 0
> cpu0 34786 0 3094 189892 413 0 2716 0
> cpu1 4007 0 3231 221411 2468 0 548 0

Well, I'm not sure whether to be happy or sad. Thanks for checking.=20

